ents_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petebacondarwin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# 🐞 bug report\r\n\r\n### Affected Package\r\n\r\n@angular/compiler-cli\r\n\r\n### Is this a regression?\r\n\r\nTechnically, no, but things like this used to work just fine with older versions of Angular.\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nOftentimes, running npm install is a long pole task when running CI/CD jobs. In my case, I have a monorepo from which I build many libraries. I have a pipeline that has a prepare stage/job, which runs npm install into a common node_modules directory, and then I spawn about 20 different jobs in parallel which build the libraries. Currently, things are not working well with Angular 10 because the lock file path is hard-coded into the node_modules directory, and ngcc seems to randomly fail when it sometimes finds a lock file already in place.\r\n\r\nThe location of the lock file is hard-coded in https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/d1ea1f4c7f3358b730b0d94e65b00bc28cae279c/packages/compiler-cli/ngcc/src/locking/lock_file.ts#L11\r\n\r\nIt would be great if this could either be configurable, or not inside node_modules, but instead in a tmp directory near where the ng build command is being executed.\r\n\r\n## 🔥 Exception or Error\r\n\r\nError: Lock found, but no process with PID 40 seems to be running.\r\n(If you are sure no ngcc process is running then you should delete the lock-file at /builds/core-build/vmw-ngx-components/node_modules/@angular/compiler-cli/ngcc/__ngcc_lock_file__.)\r\n    at new TimeoutError (/builds/core-build/vmw-ngx-components/node_modules/@angular/compiler-cli/ngcc/src/locking/async_locker.js:18:51)\r\n    at AsyncLocker.<anonymous> (/builds/core-build/vmw-ngx-components/node_modules/@angular/compiler-cli/ngcc/src/locking/async_locker.js:111:47)\r\n    at step (/builds/core-build/vmw-ngx-components/node_modules/tslib/tslib.js:140:27)\r\n    at Object.next (/builds/core-build/vmw-ngx-components/node_modules/tslib/tslib.js:121:57)\r\n    at /builds/core-build/vmw-ngx-components/node_modules/tslib/tslib.js:114:75\r\n    at new Promise (<anonymous>)\r\n    at Object.__awaiter (/builds/core-build/vmw-ngx-components/node_modules/tslib/tslib.js:110:16)\r\n    at AsyncLocker.create (/builds/core-build/vmw-ngx-components/node_modules/@angular/compiler-cli/ngcc/src/locking/async_locker.js:68:28)\r\n    at AsyncLocker.<anonymous> (/builds/core-build/vmw-ngx-components/node_modules/@angular/compiler-cli/ngcc/src/locking/async_locker.js:51:59)\r\n    at step (/builds/core-build/vmw-ngx-components/node_modules/tslib/tslib.js:140:27)\r\nAn unhandled exception occurred: NGCC failed.\r\n\r\n## 🌍  Your Environment\r\n\r\n**Angular Version:**\r\n\r\n10","closed_by":{"login":"alxhub","id":4175141,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxNzUxNDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4175141?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alxhub","html_url":"https://github.com/alxhub","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alxhub/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alxhub/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alxhub/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alxhub/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alxhub/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alxhub/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alxhub/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alxhub/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alxhub/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/